e offset is always a multiple of `gcd(3600, 2^32) = 16`, so `modified_time` always fits in `int32`.\n\n**Result:** `src/lib.rs` needed **no changes** — the translation was already byte-exact, including the `cvttsd2si` INT_MIN emulation, `int`-width offset arithmetic in `get_modified_time`, the `switch` fall-through chain, and the C-truncating `%` semantics. All of `--no-default-features`, default, `--all-features`, `--release`, and both rustc optimization levels pass (`./scripts/verify.sh`). Nothing in `c_src/` was modified."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1123,"cache_read_input_tokens":179377,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1123,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"36039f30-fd09-4c4d-8331-c2e5578be93e","uuid":"dcedb916-f635-4fa1-a95f-78322c9c334d","timestamp":"2026-08-19T22:42:05.871Z"}
